    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_53"/>
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DataObjectReference_53" name="Case and channel [observed]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_53">
      <bpmn:documentation>Corrected event CSV: CaseId, Activity, Actor; order channel comes from the source file. No customer identity or timestamp is available. Sales IDs are not case IDs.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_54"/>
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DataObjectReference_54" name="Pizza type / size [source fields]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_54">
      <bpmn:documentation>The Sales worksheets record Pizza Type and Pizza Size. Using those fields as a preparation specification is an authored information-flow assumption; there is no row-level sales-to-case join.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataStoreReference id="DataStoreReference_55" name="Price catalogue [source]">
      <bpmn:documentation>PizzasInfo: 18 type/size entries, recorded cost and revenue. Monetary unit is unspecified. The association with settlement describes a proposed information interface, not a recorded data exchange.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataStoreReference>
    <bpmn:dataStoreReference id="DataStoreReference_56" name="Recorded sales [source]">
      <bpmn:documentation>Sales fields: Id, StructureId, Pizza Type, Pizza Size, Revenue, Cost, Satisfaction, Weekday, Customer Location, Customer Type. This is a sales record, not proof of a distinct customer or an event-log transaction. Cached Excel values are used; formulas are never executed.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataStoreReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_57"/>
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="DataObjectReference_57" name="Customer location [source field]" dataObjectRef="DataObject_57">
      <bpmn:documentation>Customer Location is a geographic category in Sales, not a street address or a case-linked delivery instruction. Its proposed use in planning is an explicit modeling assumption.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
